@startuml seq-ch1-reliable
title ch1 reliable-ordered channel - sliding window IN libnetpak (relay stays dumb)

participant "Game A" as GA
participant "libnetpak A\n(ch1 window)" as LA
participant "relay" as R
participant "libnetpak B\n(ch1 window)" as LB
participant "Game B" as GB

GA -> LA : netpak_send(B, ch1, msg1, RELIABLE)
LA -> LA : assign seq=1, hold copy in window
LA -> R : DATA ch1 {seq=1}
R -> LB : forward (fire-and-forget - relay unaware of reliability)
LB -> LB : in-order? deliver; record ack=1
LB --> GB : netpak_recv -> msg1

GA -> LA : send msg2 (seq=2)
LA -> R : DATA ch1 {seq=2}
R -x LB : LOST

GA -> LA : send msg3 (seq=3)
LA -> R : DATA ch1 {seq=3}
R -> LB : forward
LB -> LB : seq gap (expected 2) - buffer msg3,\nack still = 1

LB -> R : DATA ch1 {ack=1} (piggybacked on reverse traffic\nor bare ack after delay)
R -> LA : forward
... RTO ~250 ms (doubling) expires for seq=2 ...
LA -> R : DATA ch1 {seq=2} RETRANSMIT
R -> LB : forward
LB -> LB : gap filled - deliver 2 then buffered 3, ack=3
LB --> GB : netpak_recv -> msg2, msg3 (in order)
LB -> R : {ack=3}
R -> LA : forward
LA -> LA : window slides; copies 1-3 released
note over LA,LB : identical code path over a physical\nadapter - reliability ships in the ROM
@enduml
